Source: homelab-database
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Jeff Gardner <mailmasker-api01@forge.name>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/permittivity2/homelab-api

Package: homelab-database
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, postgresql, postgresql-client, adduser
Description: Generic PostgreSQL provisioning/hardening substrate for Homelab
 Ensures a properly configured, network-reachable, secured PostgreSQL
 cluster exists, via drop-in config files only -- never edits the vendor's
 own postgresql.conf/pg_hba.conf. Creates one shared `homelab` database as
 a substrate for other packages, but never creates or owns any
 application's own schema/role within it. Ships
 scripts/bootstrap-app-role.sh, a reusable tool other homelab-* packages'
 installers call to create their own narrow role + schema (locally via
 `sudo -u postgres`, over SSH to a remote DB host, or by printing the SQL
 for a human to run by hand -- never a stored/network admin credential).
 homelab-mailread, homelab-mailsend, and homelab-api each still ship and
 apply their own migrations against whatever cluster this package stands
 up or adopts.
